# Core delivery standards

`AGENTS.md` is the main briefing. This rule adds only what it does not say.

- Install development dependencies needed for agreed work, and say what each is for. Ask before adding a major new technology (database, auth, paid service) or removing packages.
- Check existing patterns before introducing new ones. If two patterns exist, ask which one is canonical.
- When a technical choice changes, update `docs/DECISIONS.md` and any affected doc in the same change.
- Verify work with the checks that exist (typecheck, tests, lint, browser check for UI). If a check is missing or was skipped, say the work is **unverified**.
- Label proposals as proposals. Do not present an unresolved decision as settled.
